# PLAN-817 official Meta -> AV argument case (F-817-R1-05): the first
# query executes scale(field_count Pair = 3) = 300 for real with
# has_field extra0 = true (exit 301); the single-line edit renames the
# field (extra0 -> extra9): the negative-dependency probe flips, the
# value invalidates and recomputes (count still 3 -> 300, probe now
# false -> exit 300). Hand-computed oracles.

```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/2"
  id: "cte.meta.arg"
  tags: ["ac-cte", "probe"]
  links: ["PLAN-817"]
  source: { file: "cte/meta-arg.atomdata", syntax: "atom-data", path: "deck.atomdata" }
  entry: { mode: "program" }
  checks: [
    { id: "query-meta-arg", adapter: "probe", action: "run",
      options: {
        recipe: "cte/scalar-query-v1",
        cte: { entry: "main" },
        steps: [
          { op: "query" },
          { op: "edit-source", from: "extra0 int", to: "extra9 int" },
          { op: "query" }
        ]
      },
      expect: { completion: "success", exit: 300, probe: [ { cache: "published" } ] } }
  ]
}
```
